   "text": "Objects (OOP)"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What is an object?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- An **object** is a representation of a real-world entity eg teacher, aeroplane, mobile phone, cat etc\n- A **class** is like a blueprint that describes the properties and behaviours of objects, while an **object** is a specific instance created based on that blueprint with its own unique values for the properties\n- A constructor is a special **method** within a class that is automatically called when an **object** of that class is created  (***instantiated***)\n- **Constructors** typically define the initial values of** instance variables** and perform any necessary setup to prepare the **object** for use"
